0.11.2
 - fix: `python -m chipstream.cli` failed with ModuleNotFoundError
 - fix: `chipstream-cli --recursive` silently did nothing when PATH_IN is a file
 - fix: malformed `-ks`/`-kb`/`-kf`/`-kg` arguments of `chipstream-cli` caused
   tracebacks; values could not contain "=" and "None" was not accepted
 - fix: `chipstream-cli --recursive` stopped at the first file that failed and
   aborted when an output file already existed; now it continues, reports
   failed files, and skips files with existing output
 - fix: invalid `--limit-events` values of `chipstream-cli` caused misleading
   errors or tracebacks; open ranges (e.g. `5-n`) and values beyond the dataset
   size are now supported
 - enh: cache compiled PyTorch models persistently in the user cache directory
   (`TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR`, only if writable and not set already), so that
   compiling a model with the "inductor" backend is much faster in later runs
 - enh: add a button for removing segmentation models from the list (#11)
 - enh: show the system-wide CPU and RAM usage in the status bar (#1)
 - enh: expert settings (Settings menu) for additional keyword arguments of the
   pipeline steps in the GUI, with a warning in the status bar while they are
   active (#12)
 - enh: sort the list of segmentation models by name (case-insensitive,
   numbers by value)
 - enh: pause button for pausing and resuming the analysis by suspending the
   worker processes (#9)
 - enh: show the utilization and memory usage of NVIDIA GPUs in the status
   bar (via nvidia-ml-py)
 - setup: bump dcnum to 0.31.3 (limit `index_mapping` to the dataset size)
 - setup: add `nvidia-ml-py` to the `gui` extra
 - build: remove the splash screen workaround (`_PYIBoot_SPLASH`) and require PyInstaller>=6.10 for Windows builds, which fixed the splash screen reappearing in child processes (#7)
 - ref: fix all ruff findings (also in tests and build-recipes)
 - ref: fix pyright findings in the CLI and in `detect_flickering` calls
 - ref: fix pyright findings in the GUI; exclude the generated `*_ui.py`
   files from pyright
 - ref: move parsing of `KEY=VALUE` keyword arguments from the CLI to
   `chipstream.kwargs_parse` (no click dependency)
